## 1) README.md (root)

````markdown
# Microservices CI/CD Example (Jenkins + Kubernetes)

Three simple Node.js microservices:
- auth-service
- user-service
- payment-service

CI: Jenkins (Jenkinsfile included)
Container registry: Docker Hub or AWS ECR (set env vars)
Kubernetes: any cluster (minikube, kind, EKS)

## Quickstart (local)
1. Build and run locally:
   ```bash
   docker-compose up --build
````

2. Visit:

   * [http://localhost:3001/auth/health](http://localhost:3001/auth/health)
   * [http://localhost:3002/user/health](http://localhost:3002/user/health)
   * [http://localhost:3003/payment/health](http://localhost:3003/payment/health)

## Jenkins setup (high level)

* Install Jenkins with Docker & kubectl access.
* Add credentials (DOCKER_REGISTRY, DOCKER_USERNAME, DOCKER_PASSWORD, KUBECONFIG content or mount).
* Create a Multibranch Pipeline pointing to this repo (or a Pipeline job if single branch).
* Pipeline reads `Jenkinsfile` at repo root.

## Deployment

Jenkins builds images, tags them with build number or Git SHA, pushes to registry, updates k8s manifest (IMAGE_TAG) and runs `kubectl apply`.

See `Jenkinsfile` for exact pipeline steps.

````

