## 2) Example service (auth-service)
`services/auth-service/package.json`
```json
{
  "name": "auth-service",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "main": "server.js",
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node server.js",
    "test": "echo \"no tests\""
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "^4.18.2"
  }
}
````

`services/auth-service/server.js`

```js
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
const port = process.env.PORT || 8080;

app.get('/auth/health', (req, res) => res.json({status: 'ok', service: 'auth'}));
app.get('/auth', (req, res) => res.json({message: 'auth-service'}));

app.listen(port, () => console.log(`auth-service listening on ${port}`));
```

`services/auth-service/Dockerfile`

```Dockerfile
FROM node:18-alpine
WORKDIR /app
COPY package.json ./
RUN npm install --production
COPY . .
ENV PORT=8080
EXPOSE 8080
CMD ["npm","start"]
```

Duplicate this structure for `user-service` (routes `/user/health`, port 8081) and `payment-service` (routes `/payment/health`, port 8082). Update ports in Dockerfiles and server.js accordingly.

